There is different CO2 contamination content associated with the gas phase of those oil accumulations (Fig. 13B). The Berbig˜ao reservoirs have the lowest contamination, ranging from 0.1 to 3.37 . There is a slight internal variation, since southern Berbig˜ao (well 4-BRSA-1226 RJS) shows decreasing CO2 contamination with depth, indicating local compositional gradation, while the other wells do not show a clear trend despite having a slight difference between them. The Sururu reservoirs have high variability of CO2 content, ranging from 23.5 to 33.5 , associated with a negative correlation also indicating compositional gradation. With the exception of the sample from the Itapema reservoir
